  26:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****   ==============================================================================
  27:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****                      ##### How to use this driver #####
  28:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****   ==============================================================================
  29:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****     [..]
  30:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****       The LPTIM HAL driver can be used as follows:
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccCFMTgI.s 			page 2


  31:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c **** 
  32:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****       (#)Initialize the LPTIM low level resources by implementing the
  33:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****         HAL_LPTIM_MspInit():
  34:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++) Enable the LPTIM interface clock using __HAL_RCC_LPTIMx_CLK_ENABLE().
  35:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++) In case of using interrupts (e.g. HAL_LPTIM_PWM_Start_IT()):
  36:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****              (+++) Configure the LPTIM interrupt priority using HAL_NVIC_SetPriority().
  37:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****              (+++) Enable the LPTIM IRQ handler using HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ().
  38:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****              (+++) In LPTIM IRQ handler, call HAL_LPTIM_IRQHandler().
  39:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c **** 
  40:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****       (#)Initialize the LPTIM HAL using HAL_LPTIM_Init(). This function
  41:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          configures mainly:
  42:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++) The instance: LPTIM1 or LPTIM2.
  43:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++) Clock: the counter clock.
  44:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****              (+++) Source   : it can be either the ULPTIM input (IN1) or one of
  45:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****                               the internal clock; (APB, LSE, LSI or MSI).
  46:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****              (+++) Prescaler: select the clock divider.
  47:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++)  UltraLowPowerClock : To be used only if the ULPTIM is selected
  48:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****                as counter clock source.
  49:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****              (+++) Polarity:   polarity of the active edge for the counter unit
  50:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****                                if the ULPTIM input is selected.
  51:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****              (+++) SampleTime: clock sampling time to configure the clock glitch
  52:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****                                filter.
  53:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++) Trigger: How the counter start.
  54:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****              (+++) Source: trigger can be software or one of the hardware triggers.
  55:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****              (+++) ActiveEdge : only for hardware trigger.
  56:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****              (+++) SampleTime : trigger sampling time to configure the trigger
  57:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****                                 glitch filter.
  58:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++) OutputPolarity : 2 opposite polarities are possible.
  59:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++) UpdateMode: specifies whether the update of the autoreload and
  60:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****               the compare values is done immediately or after the end of current
  61:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****               period.
  62:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++) Input1Source: Source selected for input1 (GPIO or comparator output).
  63:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++) Input2Source: Source selected for input2 (GPIO or comparator output).
  64:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****               Input2 is used only for encoder feature so is used only for LPTIM1 instance.
  65:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c **** 
  66:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****       (#)Six modes are available:
  67:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c **** 
  68:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++) PWM Mode: To generate a PWM signal with specified period and pulse,
  69:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          call HAL_LPTIM_PWM_Start() or HAL_LPTIM_PWM_Start_IT() for interruption
  70:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          mode.
  71:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c **** 
  72:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++) One Pulse Mode: To generate pulse with specified width in response
  73:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          to a stimulus, call HAL_LPTIM_OnePulse_Start() or
  74:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          HAL_LPTIM_OnePulse_Start_IT() for interruption mode.
  75:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c **** 
  76:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++) Set once Mode: In this mode, the output changes the level (from
  77:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          low level to high level if the output polarity is configured high, else
  78:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          the opposite) when a compare match occurs. To start this mode, call
  79:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          HAL_LPTIM_SetOnce_Start() or HAL_LPTIM_SetOnce_Start_IT() for
  80:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          interruption mode.
  81:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c **** 
  82:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++) Encoder Mode: To use the encoder interface call
  83:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          HAL_LPTIM_Encoder_Start() or HAL_LPTIM_Encoder_Start_IT() for
  84:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          interruption mode. Only available for LPTIM1 instance.
  85:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c **** 
  86:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++) Time out Mode: an active edge on one selected trigger input rests
  87:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          the counter. The first trigger event will start the timer, any
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccCFMTgI.s 			page 3


  88:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          successive trigger event will reset the counter and the timer will
  89:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          restart. To start this mode call HAL_LPTIM_TimeOut_Start_IT() or
  90:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          HAL_LPTIM_TimeOut_Start_IT() for interruption mode.
  91:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c **** 
  92:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          (++) Counter Mode: counter can be used to count external events on
  93:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          the LPTIM Input1 or it can be used to count internal clock cycles.
  94:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          To start this mode, call HAL_LPTIM_Counter_Start() or
  95:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****          HAL_LPTIM_Counter_Start_IT() for interruption mode.
  96:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c **** 
  97:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c **** 
  98:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****       (#) User can stop any process by calling the corresponding API:
  99:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****           HAL_LPTIM_Xxx_Stop() or HAL_LPTIM_Xxx_Stop_IT() if the process is
 100:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****           already started in interruption mode.
 101:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c **** 
 102:Drivers/STM32L4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32l4xx_hal_lptim.c ****       (#) De-initialize the LPTIM peripheral using HAL_LPTIM_DeInit().
